# held/civil/staff: the staff (art weapon 4) carried upright in the hand at rest (PROPS, P2b; P2c draws it swung): a dark
# wooden shaft with a brass collar under a carved claw that holds an orb in the person's accent colour (a mage's gold, a
# priest's own). 30 px with its head (STYLE_P2 11). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. It rides the grip (the near fist's top-left,
# the arm's hand mark), so it swings and bobs with the hand; on the held channel it shows wherever a clip leaves `held`
# unnamed (LOCO, RUN) and gives way to the swing maps where one names it; `drop` lies by a corpse's hand. The fingers
# wrap over the shaft (the hand over the grip: regions H, so gloves take them). Front: upright through the fist's outer
# half; back: beside the fist, behind the body; right: through the fist, leaning forward 3 in 5 so its head stands clear in
# front of the face; left (the far hand, hidden): the same lean behind the body, the head in front of the face, the foot
# behind. (P2b fix B10-CIVIL-STAFF-RUN-ATLAS) front and back sit a column nearer the body than they did (the widest scholar's
# LOCO stays in 128 KB), and in the run (the flag run) the side views hand over to staff_run.pxm / staff_runl.pxm, which
# carry it per swing of the arm (the right and left `when run` views below draw nothing).
use person
body man woman
role held staff
layer neck
anchor grip
keys held
z 40

